  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At the back of Rotten Mud Mountain he fights a mature brown bear while his grandfather watches. He is fifteen or sixteen, uses movement Gu and sword qi Gu, and recognizes muddy Gu when Ni Kun tosses it to him. After trapping the bear he says Ni Kun staged the fight to push him from sword path toward Ni clan’s earth path specialty, and he answers that he likes sword qi and finds earth path lame.",
      "chapters": [
        1034
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_rotten_mud_mountain",
        "sys_movement_gu",
        "gu_sword_qi_gu",
        "char_ni_kun",
        "fac_ni_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is only five and a half feet tall. His eyes shine with vigor, and he faces the bear without fear.",
      "chapters": [
        1034
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Qi Zai’s first mudman reconstruction from Rotten Mud Mountain grudge qi names itself Ni Jian before Qi Zai mishears and destroys it.",
      "chapters": [
        1036
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "young-clan-leader",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qi_zai"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rebuilt again, the mudman answers clearly as Ni Jian, young clan leader of the village and grandson of the Ni clan leader. He lost his parents young, was raised by his grandfather, and after the village slaughter his soul is taken while deep grudge remains.",
      "chapters": [
        1037
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "young-clan-leader",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Qi Zai expands a mud ball into Ni Jian’s shape. Narration places him as originally only a rank two Gu Master who, after dying to the beast group, was revived as a mudman from a mud monster corpse, with strength risen to desolate beast level matching ordinary rank six Gu Immortals. He charges Fang Yuan in hatred for forcing his grandfather’s death and slaughtering the clan, but lacks battle experience and is slowed by frost palms.",
      "chapters": [
        1040
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mudman-form",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Much later Feng Tian Yu reports finding the mudman Ni Jian, learning the village slaughter story by asking one question at a time, and noting near-immortal strength that has weakened over time.",
      "chapters": [
        2126
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mudman-found-and-restored",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_feng_tian_yu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He raises the mud monster by feeding mud Gu materials and brings it to Rotten Mud Mountain, where Ni Jian recovers strength only by increasing earth path dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        2128
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mudman-found-and-restored",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
